Separate per-user configuration administration from installation-operator permission to create commands, Python hooks, filesystem access, host-secret references or privileged network destinations. Restrict subprocess environment inheritance and credential-provider namespaces; block local/internal HTTP destinations unless explicitly allowed by host policy. Acceptance: a valid but accidentally admitted OAuth user cannot launch code, read environment/files, reference another owner's or service secrets, self-grant operator rights, or use a local HTTP upstream to bypass isolation. Test service-layer/API/MCP bypass attempts, not only UI.
